1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,680
I've already written down your answer

2
00:00:02,730 --> 00:00:03,550
The answer is already
in this envelope!

3
00:00:03,600 --> 00:00:07,920
Think of any
three-digit number
(first and last digits at least 2 apart)

4
00:00:07,970 --> 00:00:15,290
Reverse it, then subtract
the smaller number from the bigger one

5
00:00:15,340 --> 00:00:18,060
Reverse that answer
and add the two together

6
00:00:18,110 --> 00:00:21,550
Need more time?
Press and hold the screen to pause

7
00:00:22,300 --> 00:00:26,550
Done?
Your answer is…

8
00:00:26,600 --> 00:00:28,570
Your answer is…
1089!

9
00:00:28,620 --> 00:00:29,670
If I got it right,
comment "1089"!

10
00:00:29,720 --> 00:00:31,090
How did I know?

11
00:00:31,140 --> 00:00:33,960
Whatever number you pick…

12
00:00:34,010 --> 00:00:35,730
it's always 1089!

13
00:00:35,780 --> 00:00:39,170
After subtracting, there are
only 8 possible answers

14
00:00:39,220 --> 00:00:41,490
The middle digit is always 9,
and the two ends add up to 9

15
00:00:41,540 --> 00:00:43,820
Add it to its reverse,
column by column…

16
00:00:43,870 --> 00:00:46,390
Ends make 9, the middle makes 18:
900 + 180 + 9 = 1089, every time!

17
00:00:46,440 --> 00:00:50,350
Now you're the magician! Secretly write 1089 on paper,
have someone do the steps, then unfold it!

18
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:53,350
NEXT: The number you think of vanishes, and only 4 is left?
